  "$sources": [
    "The species: Punica granatum L., shi liu: a deciduous shrub or small tree 2-7 m, the branchlets angled, the short ones ending in spines; leaves oblong-lanceolate 2-9 cm by 1-2 cm, shining; flowers 1-5 at the branch ends, the calyx tube and the crumpled petals red-orange, the petals 1.5-3 cm; flowering May to July (Flora of China (Wu Zhengyi, P. H. Raven and Hong Deyuan, eds., Science Press and Missouri Botanical Garden, 1994-2013), vol. 13, Lythraceae).",
    "Habit: the tree grower's shrubby small tree, for the pomegranates in their glazed tubs (the Chenghuai sheet: 1.9 m, crown radii 0.75 and 0.55), several stems from the pot.",
    "Colours: the young leaves' bronze-tinted green and the flowers' scarlet."
